But what about your own squiddy wishes?

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:31.030
This is good enough for me.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:31.830
Yeah.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:35.690
Our biggest wish is for you to be happy.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.820
Thank you.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:44.420
I ink your wishes will be heard.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.930
Now I can rest easy and write that 
I want to eat an ocean of shrimp!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.440
You're unbelievable.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.000
I wanna eat oceans of shrimp

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.850
So you finally got it written down.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:56.870
It only took a whole 
day of slacking off.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:57.980
What's wrong?

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.590
I wish for world peace

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.590
I wish that war would 
disappear from this world

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.870
Here's a wish for world peace.

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.940
I wish everyone who's suffering 
in the world could be saved

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.940
World peace

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.940
I wish we lived in a peaceful world

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:00.940
Here too!

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:04.650
The more I look, the more 
wishes I see for world peace!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:07.400
Our wishes for the invasion are going to get

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.820
totally destroyed by these wishes!

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:12.340
Well, your wish was that 
you want to eat more shrimp.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:14.440
This is tenterrible!

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.460
You know, Squid Girl,

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.900
happiness comes in all shapes and sizes

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.450
and there are some people who are happy

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.630
I wish my grandpa's leg 
would get better

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.630
My family's good health

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:25.000
from seeing others be happy.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.800
I wish my grandma would get 
out of the hospital soon

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.800
...to be healthy.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.800
I pray my son will come home safely

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.130
I'm sure all of that sounded nice,

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.350
but actually a lot of people's 
wishes are really selfish.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:35.410
"I wish Squid Girl will always work for us."

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:35.980
I wish Squid Girl will always 
work for us - Chizuru Aizawa

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:39.600
We wish to examine Squid Girl 
- Top of the class at MIT, 
Harris, Clark, Martin

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:39.600
"We wish to examine Squid Girl"

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:43.320
I want to be united 
with Squiddie 
- Sanae Nagatsuki

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.320
"I want to be united with Squiddie"

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.570
I want to know what's 
inside the Squid hat.
 - Cindy

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:46.330
"I want to know what's 
inside the Squid hat. "

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.280
Squid no!!!!

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:57.310
Huh?

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.800
Are you changing your wish?

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:02.740
I asked for too much.

00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:06.090
There's only one thing this squid wants.

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:11.970
I wish to be safe. 
- Squid Girl

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:16.200
I finished all my summer homework!

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:18.240
Now I can do whatever I want!

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:23.860
<b>A squiddle playtime alone?!</b>

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.490
Hello?

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:28.360
Matsumoto here.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.400
Yuuta?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.810
Takeru?

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:32.490
Do you have time to hang out?

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.370
I wish I did!

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.450
My mom's being really 
annoying about my homework.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:38.410
Sorry.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:39.250
No problem.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.500
Sorry, I've got cram school today.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.420
Sorry...

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.500
Actually...

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.050
You have reached the 
answering machine of...

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.740
Just when I'm finally able 
to play all I want...

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:53.420
I don't know what to do all by myself.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.900
Why don't you watch a squiddle TV
 if you don't have anyone to play with?

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.160
Squid Girlie!

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.180
It's still morning though.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.370
There's nothing good on TV right now.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.020
Don't be so squiddy sure.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.520
It's a shogi show.

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:10.150
Do you know anything about shogi?

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.090
Ten seconds.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.490
What was so funny about that?

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:20.320
His voice sounded so funny 
when he said "ten seconds"!

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.550
And we'll be seeing a tropical 
low pressure system in this area...

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:27.630
And if you act now, you'll also get...

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:30.760
Can't... squidding... breathe!

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:31.800
Is it that funny?

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.610
As long as you've got a TV,

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.420
you'll never be bored, 
even if you're all alone!

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:39.450
I envy you.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:40.810
Hey.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.180
Eiko!

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.690
Watching TV this early in the morning 
is pure poison for the body!

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:49.230
The weather's nice, 
so why don't you play outside?

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:51.110
I ink you're right.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.330
Want to come with us?

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:55.660
I've got some important 
stuff to get done.

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:58.650
We're gonna jet.

00:16:58.650 --> 00:16:59.600
Bye!

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:00.570
Okay.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:03.650
Well, then.

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:05.870
Time to play that new game I just got!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.040
It's hot today, again.

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:12.520
It's hard to figure out what to 
do when you're alone outside.

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:13.760
That's not true.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:17.980
This wall thing is the ultimate partner!

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:19.600
Walls are tentacularly great.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:22.360
They're quiet as a clam,

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:25.450
but if you throw something at them,
 they send it right back.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:27.640
Like this!

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.160
The only downside is

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:33.740
that there's no good place 
to direct your anger.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.570
Our yard's a little too small 
to play against the wall.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.530
Then why don't we go to the park?

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:39.280
Park?

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.040
We're here!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.340
But isn't a park exactly the kind

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:44.460
of place where you play 
with a lot of people?

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:46.900
It doesn't have to be.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:48.580
Look around, Takeru!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.110
There's someone reading 
alone in the shade.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:52.730
There's someone running.

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:54.920
There's someone staring 
off into the distance.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:58.180
Everyone's having fun in 
their own squiddle way!

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.140
You're right.

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:03.150
But that person doesn't look like 
he's really having fun.

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:04.820
Is he crying?

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:07.060
Being an adult sure is hard.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:08.460
What's wrong?

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:09.460
N-nothing!

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:11.830
I was just thinking how great you are.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.320
I always get so caught up in 
playing with my friends,

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:18.610
I didn't even know that there are all 
these other ways to have fun!

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:24.830
I guess I only started playing with 
others once I set tentacle on land.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:27.160
But that means I've learned

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:31.670
to play alone, no matter the circumstances!

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:34.920
You could call me the 
Play Alone Squidmeister!

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:39.790
So stuff you can do alone 
in a park includes...

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:42.370
Hey, where are you going?

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.500
This is really exsquidsite!

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.060
It's important to be able 
to have fun with anything.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:50.190
Takeru!

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:54.270
I'm sure you could find a way to 
play alone, too, if you just look!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.150
Yeah!

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:59.130
Then why don't we both find 
ways to play by ourselves?

00:18:59.130 --> 00:18:59.710
Huh?

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:02.000
If you just depend on me all the time,

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:06.150
you'll never become a true 
Play Alone Squidmeister like me!

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:07.320
I see.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:08.410
Okay.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.000
I'm going to try too.

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:31.940
And now, for a little break.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.700
Owww...

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.950
You squiddle...!

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:45.900
How dare this lowly ant attack me?!

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:47.710
Wait a sec.

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:50.710
I bet this ant is going back 
to his secret base right now.

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:55.130
If I follow him,
 I can squid-vade his base!

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.240
Squid Girlie looks like she's having fun.

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:00.870
What am I going to do?

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:03.370
I can't think of anything.

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:04.820
He's so slow.

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:06.360
Now he's trying to take 
food back with him,

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:08.850
and it's slowing him down even more.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.030
Come on, Ant-taro! 
Hurry up.

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:14.030
You still have a long way to go.

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:17.330
Hey, those look like his friends.

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:19.360
We must be squidding
close to the secret base.

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.980
The squid-vasion is about to begin.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.090
Hey, what are you doing?

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.780
I thought all of you were friends!

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:33.460
Looks like Ant-taro has lost this one...

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:38.160
They look the same, but I guess 
they weren't friends after all.

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.530
There's some here, too!

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:41.640
You're right!

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:43.800
Here we go!

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.010
Those boys!

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:51.570
Now they're stuck!

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:52.940
Hey you!

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:57.100
Knock it the squid off!

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:58.590
It's some weird girl!

00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.770
Run for it!

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.820
I won't let you off the hook next time!

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:04.210
Look, Ant-taro.

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:07.240
Now you can go home.

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:18.420
I'm so squidding glad.

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:24.160
You're not alone anymore.

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.740
Squid Girl!

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:28.330
Let's go home!

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:29.870
It's getting dark.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:31.100
You're right.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:35.960
Kids these days are tenterrible.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:39.360
Aren't you the one who wanted 
to invade them first?

00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:41.280
What did you do today, Takeru?

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:45.390
Squid Girlie was trying to teach 
me how to play by myself.

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:47.720
I was still thinking about how 
to do it when it got dark though.

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:49.760
You've still got a lot to learn.

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:52.990
You've got a long way to go until you 
become a Play Alone Squidmeister.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:53.840
Yeah.

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.430
You're really good at it, Squid Girlie.

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:58.520
Oh, stop.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:00.950
Hey guys...

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:04.650
If you went together, why didn't you 
just play with each other?

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.250
I guess we could've squidding done that.

00:23:40.530 --> 00:23:42.450
I protect all people from accidents at sea!

00:23:42.450 --> 00:23:45.130
I'm the lifeguard of justice, 
Goro Arashiyama!

00:23:45.130 --> 00:23:45.880
Next up are:

00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:47.360
Run, Squid, Run?!

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:48.850
Ink that an SP?!

00:23:48.850 --> 00:23:51.160
Wanna go on an esquidpade?!

00:23:51.470 --> 00:23:53.650
Never skip your stretches!
